# ===========================================================================
# ThirdParty .gitignore
#
# Source/ holds the vendored libraries, each a faithful copy of its upstream
# release. This file only drops the parts of those releases the engine never
# builds.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SDL's examples and test suite are not vendored -- 450 files and ~17 MB that
# this engine never builds.
#
# Both are gated in SDL's own CMakeLists, and both gates are forced OFF in
# ThirdParty/CMakeLists.txt: add_subdirectory(examples) happens only under
# if(SDL_EXAMPLES), and add_subdirectory(test) only under if(SDL_TESTS).
# Turning either on against this checkout fails the configure with a
# missing-directory error, which is the intended outcome -- the directories
# genuinely are not here.
#
# NOT excluded, and easy to confuse with the above: src/test/. That is where
# the SDL3_test library's sources actually live (SDL globs
# src/test/*.c for it), so it stays tracked. The patterns below are anchored to
# the SDL root and do not reach it.
#
# The VisualC/ paths are the .vcxproj files that BUILD the examples and tests
# -- useless without the sources, and VisualC/VisualC/ is a nested duplicate
# that exists upstream. Every path is listed explicitly rather than as a bare
# "examples/" or "test/" pattern, which would be a standing trap for any future
# SDL directory that happens to share the name.
#
# Xcode/SDLTest is deliberately KEPT despite the name. Unlike VisualC/tests it
# is a mixed project: it builds the SDL3_test library from src/test/ as well as
# the test programs, so dropping it would take a project for code we still
# vendor. VisualC/SDL_test, the equivalent for the library alone, is kept for
# the same reason.
#
# Everything else in the SDL tree IS committed, including the 14 files SDL's
# own .gitignore would drop (the pkg-support *Config.cmake files and the .hlsl
# shader sources, which needed git add -f). A vendored dependency should be a
# faithful copy of what was extracted; filtering it through the upstream
# project's development-time ignore rules produces a tree that silently differs
# from the release and makes the next version bump diff against phantom
# changes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Source/SDL-release-3.4.16/examples/
/Source/SDL-release-3.4.16/test/
/Source/SDL-release-3.4.16/VisualC/examples/
/Source/SDL-release-3.4.16/VisualC/tests/
/Source/SDL-release-3.4.16/VisualC/VisualC/
